"comments":2,"created_at":"2018-03-14T20:00:51Z","updated_at":"2019-09-13T11:21:57Z","closed_at":"2018-03-15T18:38:53Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## I'm submitting a...\r\n<!-- Check one of the following options with \"x\" -->\r\n<pre><code>\r\n[x] Regression (a behavior that used to work and stopped working in a new release)\r\n</code></pre>\r\n\r\nREF: [b/74538140](http://b/74538140)\r\n\r\n## Current behavior\r\n\r\nA style that contains an a value with a string escape such as `'\\0025BC'` is emitted as `\"\\\\x0025BC\"` instead of the expected \"\\0025BC\".\r\n\r\nThis is true when using 2.6 or 2.7 of TypeScript but does not reproduce with 2.5.\r\n\r\nThis is related to https://github.com/Microsoft/TypeScript/issues/20192. TypeScript, beginning with 2.6, calls `escapeString` for the value of synthetic literals.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/Microsoft/TypeScript/blob/1736741e546bb6d436acd4c0632e3b23c7033b29/src/compiler/utilities.ts#L352\r\n\r\nThis produces the incorrect escaping identically had this been an interpolation.\r\n\r\n## Expected behavior\r\n\r\nThe escaped string in css should be emitted correctly.\r\n\r\n## Minimal reproduction of the problem with instructions\r\n\r\n1. `ng new repro`\r\n2. modify app.component.css to be\r\n\r\n```css\r\nspan {\r\n  content: '\\0025BC';\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n`./node_modules/.bin/ngc -p src/tsconfig.app.json`\r\n\r\nInspect `out-tsc/app/src/app/app.component.css.shim.ngstyle.js`\r\n\r\n**EXPECTED**\r\n\r\n\r\n```\r\n[\"span[_ngcontent-%COMP%] {\\n  content: '\\\\0025BC';\\n}\"]\r\n```\r\n\r\n**RECEIVED**\r\n\r\n```\r\n[\"span[_ngcontent-%COMP%] {\\n  content: '\\\\x00025BC';\\n}\"]\r\n```\r\n\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"mhevery","id":111951,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMTk1MQ==","avatar_url":"ht